**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A name read through a template and written back, at the level of its text (001 §J 'It names setups and experiments, and PARSES names back to match imported data'; 'their cases become the template engine's first test cases': `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:parsed`) reads the lab's labels by `experimentRegex` and `objectRegex` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:experimentRegex`, `:objectRegex`), and step 270 re-points its callers here). In `NamingTemplates.fs`, after step 268's declarations; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `NameText of string` with `.value`: a whole name as text, a setup's or an experiment's name or a label a lab file carries. (2) `SlotPart = { role : SlotRole; part : NamePart }`, `ObjectAngle = { position : SlotPosition; angle : Angle }` and `NameReading = { parts : SlotPart list; angles : ObjectAngle list; noteOpt : NamePart option }`, the values a name holds, each list in its template's order, with `member this.tryFindPart (role : SlotRole) : NamePart option` and `member this.tryFindAngle (position : SlotPosition) : Angle option`. (3) An angle is written as its degrees rounded to three decimals, in the invariant culture, with no exponent, no trailing zero and no sign on zero (`45`, `-22.5`, `0.333`, `0`); it is read as an optional `-`, ASCII digits and an optional `.` followed by ASCII digits, and becomes `Angle.degree` of that number (`Geometry.fs:degree`). (4) Each placeholder of a template owns the literal text directly before it, back to the placeholder before it; the literal after the last placeholder is the template's tail. The optional placeholders of one object, `{obj<k>}` and `{phi<k>}`, form one group, and every other optional placeholder is a group alone. (5) `type NamingTemplate with member this.writeName (reading : NameReading) : Result<NameText, NamingTemplateError>` writes, in the template's order, each placeholder's value after the text it owns: a `SlotPlaceholder` the reading's part of its role, an `AnglePlaceholder` the angle of its position, `NotePlaceholder` the note. An optional placeholder the reading lacks is left out with the text it owns; a required one answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming the placeholder's `text`. The tail ends the name. (6) `member this.readName (name : NameText) : Result<NameReading, NamingTemplateError>` tries the ways of leaving out the optional groups in one fixed order, binary counting over the groups in template order with the last group the lowest digit and a left-out group a one: every group kept comes first, and an earlier group is kept longest. One way reads the name left to right. Each kept placeholder's owned text must stand at the reading point. Its value runs from there to the first place, at least one character on, where the text that follows it in this way stands (the next kept placeholder's owned text, or the tail), or to the end of the name when that text is empty. A value is never empty, an angle's value must read as an angle, and after the last value the rest of the name must be the tail exactly. The first way that reads answers the reading; when none does, the answer is `NameMismatchErr` naming the name and the template. The scanning is done by locals inside the members (ELEV003P, ELEV010P). No regular expression, backtracking within a way, cache or other member is added. So the lab's labels read as `parsed` reads them: `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` holds the analyzer `CPL` and the note `2`, because keeping the note is tried before leaving it out, and `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` keeps its sign, because a value runs at least one character before the next owned text. Tests, in `NamingTemplateTests` (step 268), over `NamingTemplate.standard` and each label as a `NameText`: `the lab's labels read into their source, objects, angles, analyzer and note`: `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` reads the source part `CPL` (`PrepSlotRole 1`), the objects `QZ` and `LR` with the angles 90° and 90°, the analyzer part `CPL` and no note; `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL` the object `AIR` at 0° and no second object; `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` the source `LP`, the analyzer `CPL` and the note `2`; `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR` the note `BR`; `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` the angle −45°; and `LP-(QZ#22.5)-LP` 22.5°; each angle equals `Angle.degree` of its number exactly. `a name that does not fit the template is refused naming it`: `Darkness`, `BullshitCheck`, `BullshitCheck-2`, `LP-(Darkness)-CPL2`, `CPL-(QZ#ab)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#90-LR)-CPL` and the empty name each answer `NameMismatchErr` whose reason holds the name. `writing a reading back gives the name it was read from`: for `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-LP-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR`, `LP-(LR#45)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` and `LP-(QZ#22.5)-LP`, `writeName` of the `readName` answers the same text. `a reading writes each value in its place and leaves out an optional one it lacks with the text it owns`: the test-local reading of the source `CPL`, the object `QZ` at 45° and the analyzer `CPL` writes `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`; with the note `2`, `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL-2`; with a second object `LR` at 45°, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`; an angle of 1/3° is written `0.333` and one of −0.0001° `0`; and the reading without the analyzer answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming `analyzer1`.

**Acceptance.** After names are read and written, `NameText`, `SlotPart`, `ObjectAngle` and `NameReading` MUST exist in `NamingTemplates.fs`, `NamingTemplate.readName` MUST read the lab's labels as `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed` reads them and refuse a name the template does not fit, and `writeName` MUST write a reading back to the name it was read from; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the lab's labels read into their source, objects, angles, analyzer and note`, `a name that does not fit the template is refused naming it`, `writing a reading back gives the name it was read from` and `a reading writes each value in its place and leaves out an optional one it lacks with the text it owns`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.
